  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the Urgent MHPSS Needs of the Earthquake-Affected Populations in Herat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the latest earthquake reports in Afghanistan, the number of affected households is expected. Due to ongoing concerns linked to aftershocks, a shortage of healthcare workers has been reported. Displaced survivors in Herat City and affected villages are residing in temporary shelters, such as tents. These conditions, marked by inadequate healthcare assistance and those whose underlying psychosocial issues have escalated the need for mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and psychological first aid (PFA). Through the earthquake response, IOM aims to provide psychosocial support to earthquake affected communities through mobile psychosocial teams in Herat province earthquake affected districts.</narrative>
  </description>
